alright,

893
00:25:50,930 --> 00:25:51,630
which sits on

894
00:25:51,630 --> 00:25:52,710
chromosome 11,

895
00:25:53,410 --> 00:25:54,530
gets translocated

896
00:25:54,530 --> 00:25:55,630
to the immunoglobulin

897
00:25:55,630 --> 00:25:56,650
heavy chain spot

898
00:25:56,650 --> 00:25:57,690
so that now

899
00:25:57,690 --> 00:25:58,450
what's sitting here

900
00:25:58,450 --> 00:25:59,310
is cyclin D,

901
00:25:59,690 --> 00:26:00,430
then you're going to get

902
00:26:00,430 --> 00:26:01,310
overexpression

903
00:26:01,310 --> 00:26:02,170
of cyclin D.

904
00:26:02,430 --> 00:26:02,950
And what does

905
00:26:02,950 --> 00:26:03,810
cyclin D do?

906
00:26:04,190 --> 00:26:05,350
Cyclin D allows

907
00:26:05,350 --> 00:26:06,270
the cell to go

908
00:26:06,270 --> 00:26:07,330
from the G1

909
00:26:07,330 --> 00:26:08,610
to the S phase.

910
00:26:09,490 --> 00:26:10,810
All of this is high yield.

911
00:26:10,930 --> 00:26:11,270
It shows up

912
00:26:11,270 --> 00:26:12,090
on examinations.

913
00:26:12,290 --> 00:26:12,710
What do I mean

914
00:26:12,710 --> 00:26:13,370
by all of this?

915
00:26:13,730 --> 00:26:13,850
Well,

916
00:26:13,890 --> 00:26:14,230
first of all,

917
00:26:14,290 --> 00:26:14,950
you need to know

918
00:26:14,950 --> 00:26:17,490
that in mantle cell lymphoma

919
00:26:17,490 --> 00:26:18,450
you get expansion

920
00:26:18,450 --> 00:26:19,070
of the mantle.

921
00:26:19,450 --> 00:26:19,550
So,

922
00:26:19,650 --> 00:26:20,110
for example,

923
00:26:21,530 --> 00:26:22,530
sometimes they give you

924
00:26:22,530 --> 00:26:22,970
a description

925
00:26:22,970 --> 00:26:23,670
on an examination

926
00:26:23,670 --> 00:26:24,510
where they say

927
00:26:24,510 --> 00:26:25,670
that a biopsy

928
00:26:25,670 --> 00:26:26,250
of the lymph node

929
00:26:26,250 --> 00:26:26,790
is performed

930
00:26:26,790 --> 00:26:27,850
and it shows

931
00:26:27,850 --> 00:26:29,410
expansion of the region

932
00:26:29,410 --> 00:26:30,630
next to the follicle.

933
00:26:30,990 --> 00:26:31,170
So,

934
00:26:31,270 --> 00:26:31,850
what's the region

935
00:26:31,850 --> 00:26:32,730
next to the follicle?

936
00:26:32,910 --> 00:26:33,410
The mantle.

937
00:26:33,630 --> 00:26:33,830
So,

938
00:26:33,830 --> 00:26:35,090
that's one important thing

939
00:26:35,090 --> 00:26:35,350
to know

940
00:26:35,350 --> 00:26:36,610
about mantle cell lymphoma.

941
00:26:37,010 --> 00:26:37,890
Another important thing

942
00:26:37,890 --> 00:26:38,430
you have to know

943
00:26:38,430 --> 00:26:39,530
is the translocation.

944
00:26:39,650 --> 00:26:41,410
It's an 11-14 translocation.

945
00:26:42,090 --> 00:26:42,590
You need to know

946
00:26:42,590 --> 00:26:46,410
that on chromosome 14

947
00:26:46,410 --> 00:26:47,810
is immunoglobulin heavy chain

948
00:26:47,810 --> 00:26:48,730
and that's the region

949
00:26:48,730 --> 00:26:50,870
where the translocation occurs

950
00:26:50,870 --> 00:26:53,010
and that the key gene

951
00:26:53,010 --> 00:26:54,230
that's being translocated

952
00:26:54,230 --> 00:26:55,370
is cyclin D1

953
00:26:55,370 --> 00:26:56,910
and that cyclin D1

954
00:26:56,910 --> 00:26:57,650
is important

955
00:26:57,650 --> 00:26:58,430
to go

956
00:26:58,430 --> 00:26:59,650
from the G1

957
00:26:59,650 --> 00:27:00,610
to the S phase.

958
00:27:00,830 --> 00:27:01,210
That's also

959
00:27:01,210 --> 00:27:01,670
an important

960
00:27:01,670 --> 00:27:03,590
biochemistry question.

961
00:27:03,590 --> 00:27:06,010
I remember vividly

962
00:27:06,010 --> 00:27:08,030
that on one occasion

963
00:27:08,030 --> 00:27:10,250
I tell my students

964
00:27:10,250 --> 00:27:11,390
and I'm telling you

965
00:27:11,390 --> 00:27:12,090
you're a student

966
00:27:12,090 --> 00:27:15,270
that I really see

967
00:27:15,270 --> 00:27:16,150
the board exams

968
00:27:16,150 --> 00:27:17,870
and other examinations

969
00:27:17,870 --> 00:27:18,770
if they're well written

970
00:27:18,770 --> 00:27:19,990
as thinking exams

971
00:27:19,990 --> 00:27:21,870
and one of the students

972
00:27:21,870 --> 00:27:23,270
once came up to me

973
00:27:23,270 --> 00:27:23,670
and complained

974
00:27:23,670 --> 00:27:23,990
and said

975
00:27:23,990 --> 00:27:24,710
well you know

976
00:27:24,710 --> 00:27:27,190
I had a really foolish question

977
00:27:27,190 --> 00:27:28,010
on my exam

978
00:27:28,010 --> 00:27:29,090
where someone

979
00:27:29,090 --> 00:27:30,590
where I was asked about

980
00:27:30,590 --> 00:27:32,130
you know

981
00:27:32,130 --> 00:27:33,230
on what chromosome

982
00:27:33,230 --> 00:27:34,570
is cyclin D1

983
00:27:34,570 --> 00:27:36,750
and you know

984
00:27:36,750 --> 00:27:37,990
he was arguing with me

985
00:27:37,990 --> 00:27:38,570
saying that

986
00:27:38,570 --> 00:27:39,050
well see

987
00:27:39,050 --> 00:27:39,670
that's not really

988
00:27:39,670 --> 00:27:40,550
a thinking question

989
00:27:40,550 --> 00:27:41,590
that's a nitpicky

990
00:27:41,590 --> 00:27:43,710
fact memorization question.

991
00:27:43,890 --> 00:27:44,070
Well

992
00:27:44,070 --> 00:27:45,130
actually

993
00:27:45,130 --> 00:27:45,570
in a way

994
00:27:45,570 --> 00:27:46,270
it is kind of

995
00:27:46,270 --> 00:27:47,090
a thinking question

996
00:27:47,090 --> 00:27:47,470
because

997
00:27:58,010 --> 00:27:58,810
is immunoglobulin

998
00:27:58,810 --> 00:27:59,370
heavy chain

999
00:27:59,370 --> 00:28:00,310
then you can kind of

1000
00:28:00,310 --> 00:28:00,750
go back

1001
00:28:00,750 --> 00:28:01,970
and derive from that

1002
00:28:01,970 --> 00:28:02,430
that

1003
00:28:02,430 --> 00:28:04,210
cyclin D1

1004
00:28:04,210 --> 00:28:05,470
is on chromosome 11

1005
00:28:05,470 --> 00:28:06,650
because cyclin D1

1006
00:28:06,650 --> 00:28:07,830
is this key

1007
00:28:07,830 --> 00:28:09,630
gene that's involved

1008
00:28:09,630 --> 00:28:10,650
in the 11-14

1009
00:28:10,650 --> 00:28:11,530
translocation.

1010
00:28:12,190 --> 00:28:12,790
So anyway

1011
00:28:12,790 --> 00:28:15,050
basically

1012
00:28:15,050 --> 00:28:16,030
what I want to get at

1013
00:28:16,030 --> 00:28:17,130
is the fact

1014
00:28:17,130 --> 00:28:17,790
that you do need

1015
00:28:17,790 --> 00:28:18,350
to be familiar

1016
00:28:18,350 --> 00:28:19,330
